onditions, such as kidney stones and hyperuricemia, highlighting their comprehensive approach to nutrition and health management across different populations.\",3\r\n11938,CÁLCULO RENAL,\"Cálculo renal refers to kidney stones, which are hard deposits made of minerals and salts that form inside the kidneys. These deposits can lead to significant pain and complications within the urinary tract. In summary, cálculos renales are characterized as hard mineral and salt formations in the kidneys, often resulting in discomfort and potential health issues.\",2\r\n12031,ALTERACIONES DEL PH URINARIO,Alteraciones del pH urinario refers to changes in urine pH that can affect the solubility of various substances and contribute to kidney stone formation.,1\r\n12021,BOIX GC,\"Boix GC is an author who contributed to the literature on kidney stones, specifically in the publication \"\"Litiasis Renal.\"\"\",1\r\n11947,CISTINA,Cistina is an amino acid that can lead to the formation of kidney stones in individuals with a genetic disorder known as cystinuria.,1\r\n12027,CRIBADO METABÓLICO,Cribado metabólico is a comprehensive metabolic screening process recommended for patients with a history of kidney stones to understand the underlying causes.,1\r\n11946,FOSFATO AMÓNICO MAGNÉSICO,\"Fosfato amónico magnésico, or struvite, is a type of kidney stone that often forms in the presence of urinary infections and alkaline urine.\",1\r\n11945,FOSFATO CÁLCICO,\"Fosfato cálcico, or brushite, is a type of kidney stone that forms in specific urinary pH conditions and is associated with hypercalciuria.\",1\r\n12029,HIPEROXALURIAS,\"Hiperoxalurias refers to high levels of oxalate in the urine, which can contribute to the formation of certain types of kidney stones.\",1\r\n12028,HIPOCAURIAS,\"Hipocalciurias refers to low levels of calcium in the urine, which can be a factor in the formation of kidney stones.\",1\r\n12030,HIPOCITRATURIAS,\"Hipocitraturias refers to low levels of citrate in the urine, wh